  ],
  "correct": "E",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Order the numbers first",
      "body": "<p>Write <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></math>. The median is c, the sum is zero, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Sorting turns the statistics into constraints.",
      "pitfall": "The question permits repeated real values; do not impose distinctness or positivity.",
      "pause": "Express a in terms of e and the range.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b3-l06",
          "reminder": "Sort data before using its median, range and mean."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bound the sum in terms of the median",
      "body": "<p>Express the smallest value using the largest value and the range. Compare the largest value with the median, then use the sorted order to put a lower bound on each entry in terms of the median.</p>",
      "recap": "Adding five entrywise bounds gives a bound on the total.",
      "pitfall": "A bound is valid for every allowed list, not just a symmetric guess.",
      "pause": "Derive a total-sum inequality involving the median and combine it with the given mean.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b3-l06",
          "reminder": "To bound a median, use order to bound every entry in terms of that median."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Turn the bound into a maximum",
      "body": "<p>For equality in the bound, take the bottom entries at their lower allowed values and the top entries at the median value.</p>",
      "recap": "A bound is a maximum only if a permitted list reaches it.",
      "pitfall": "Check both the original mean and the range of your proposed list.",
      "pause": "Solve your inequality for the median, then construct and verify an equality case.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p2-b3-l06",
          "reminder": "Give both an upper bound and an example attaining it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></math>. The median is c. Since the range is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></math>. Also c,d,e are each at least c.</p><p>Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>&#x02265;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>The list <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mn>8</mn><mo>&#x0002C;</mo><mtext>&#x000A0;</mtext><mn>8</mn></mrow></math> has sum zero, mean zero and range 20. Its median is 8, so the upper bound is attained.</p><p><strong>Answer E: 8.</strong></p>",
